3. STRICT NON-COMMERCIAL RESTRICTION

3.1. Absolute Prohibition of Commercial Use. Commercial Use of the Software, its Source Code, or any Derivative Work is strictly prohibited.

You must not, directly or indirectly, use, authorize, facilitate, enable, or permit another person to use the Software, its Source Code, or any Derivative Work for Commercial Use.

This prohibition applies regardless of whether the Software is modified or unmodified, distributed or privately used, provided for a fee or free of charge, or used as a primary product or as a supporting component of another activity.

3.2. Prohibited Activities. Without limiting Section 3.1, You must not:

(a) sell, rent, lease, sublicense, monetize, or otherwise commercially exploit the Software, its Source Code, or any Derivative Work;

(b) include, bundle, embed, incorporate, or distribute the Software or a Derivative Work as part of a commercial product, paid application, commercial platform, or revenue-generating offering;

(c) use, execute, deploy, access, develop with, test, or maintain the Software within a commercial entity, business environment, professional operation, or other commercial undertaking, including where the Software is used internally rather than offered to customers;

(d) use the Software to provide, support, or operate any paid service, hosted service, SaaS offering, subscription service, commercial API, consulting engagement, or other service intended to generate revenue or commercial advantage;

(e) use the Software or its Source Code in connection with advertising, monetization, commercial data processing, paid content production, or other activities intended to advance a commercial interest;

(f) use the Software or its Source Code to train, fine-tune, evaluate, benchmark, or develop any AI or machine-learning model intended for Commercial Use, including a model distributed commercially, offered through a paid service, licensed for commercial deployment, or used to generate commercial products or services;

(g) permit a third party to undertake any prohibited activity using copies, modifications, services, or access provided by You; or

(h) circumvent, disguise, restructure, or indirectly facilitate any activity that would be prohibited if performed directly by You.

3.3. No Revenue Threshold or De Minimis Exception. The restrictions in this Section apply regardless of the amount of revenue, the size of the organization, the duration or frequency of use, or whether the activity produces an immediate financial return. No minimum payment, profit, or commercial scale is required for an activity to qualify as Commercial Use.

