4.2. Complete Corresponding Source Code. Whenever You distribute or make available the Software, Object Code, or any Derivative Work, You must make the complete corresponding Source Code of the distributed work available to every Recipient, subject to the following requirements:

(a) the Source Code must include all modifications made by You or incorporated into the distributed Derivative Work;

(b) the Source Code must be provided in its complete, preferred form for making modifications, rather than solely as compiled, minified, obfuscated, or otherwise modification-obstructing material;

(c) the Source Code must be provided in a full, unencrypted, unobstructed, and reasonably usable form, without passwords, access restrictions, technical barriers, or other mechanisms that prevent a Recipient from accessing, reading, copying, or modifying it;

(d) the Source Code must include the applicable build files, scripts, configuration files, and documentation required by the definition in Section 1.3;

(e) the Source Code must be provided under ANCS-1.0, together with the original copyright notices, Prominent Attribution, and a complete copy of this License; and

(f) the Source Code must be made available at the time the corresponding Software or Derivative Work is distributed or made available, without unreasonable delay and without charging a fee specifically for access to the Source Code.

4.3. Public Availability. To satisfy Section 4.2, You must provide the Recipient with a working, direct, and reasonably accessible means of obtaining the complete Source Code. An appropriate means may include a publicly accessible source-code repository, such as a GitHub repository, or an equivalent public hosting service.

Where You distribute a copy of the Software or a Derivative Work, You must include a working repository URL or another direct source-access reference in the accompanying materials, documentation, distribution page, or other location reasonably accessible to the Recipient.

A repository link alone does not satisfy this requirement if the repository is private, incomplete, encrypted, obstructed, unavailable to the Recipient, or otherwise fails to provide the required Source Code.

4.4. No Source Concealment. You must not distribute a Derivative Work while withholding, concealing, encrypting, obfuscating, or otherwise obstructing access to its required Source Code. You must not impose additional contractual or technical restrictions that prevent recipients from exercising the rights granted by ANCS-1.0.

4.5. Downstream Rights. You must ensure that every Recipient receives the rights and obligations established by ANCS-1.0. You must not impose any additional condition that restricts a Recipient's permitted non-commercial access, study, modification, or redistribution of the Software or its Source Code.

Each subsequent distribution of a Derivative Work must preserve the same licensing terms, attribution requirements, source-availability requirements, and Non-Commercial restrictions.

4.6. Modifications and Notices. You must clearly identify modifications made by You, retain all original notices, and avoid representing Your modifications as original work created by the Author. The addition of new features, files, documentation, or other contributions does not exempt the resulting Derivative Work from this Section.

