You must promptly cease any prohibited Commercial Use and stop distributing copies that fail to comply with the mandatory Source Code, attribution, or licensing requirements. You must also take reasonable steps to remove or correct unauthorized distributions under Your control.

5.3. Unauthorized Exercise of Rights. Following termination, any further exercise of rights that were granted solely under this License is unauthorized. Such conduct may constitute copyright infringement under applicable copyright law and international copyright protections, in addition to any other claim or remedy available to the relevant rights holder.

5.4. No Automatic Cure. A breach shall not be deemed cured merely because You cease the offending conduct after termination. Reinstatement of rights requires the express written authorization of the relevant rights holder, unless reinstatement is otherwise required by applicable law.

5.5. Rights and Obligations That Survive. Termination does not extinguish any liability, claim, or remedy arising from a breach occurring before termination. Provisions that by their nature are intended to survive termination, including provisions concerning ownership, disclaimers, limitations of liability, interpretation, and enforcement, shall survive to the extent permitted by applicable law.

